metadata.description:
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ZP Suite\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A free, open-source toolkit for voiceover, dubbing, podcasts, e-learning and broadcast workflows in REAPER. It brings script reading, subtitle handling, project preparation, accessible controls and ZP audio tools into one REAPER setup.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Prefer Italian?} See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "README.it.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
README in Italian
}}}
. The Suite itself is available in Italian and English.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Choose your language\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 After installing or updating, open {\b 33 Welcome} from REAPER's Action List. Under {\b Suite language}, choose {\b English} or {\b Italiano}. This preference is saved and is independent of REAPER's own language. The {\f1 ?} help buttons open the guide in the selected Suite language.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install with ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab In REAPER, choose {\b Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Import repositories}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Add this repository URL:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 {\f1 https://github.com/capitanpaolone/zp-suite/raw/master/index.xml}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Choose {\b Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Browse packages}, search for {\b ZP}, and install {\b ZP Studio Suite} and any ZP effects you need.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Synchronize packages to receive updates.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The Suite works in a clean REAPER install. SWS, js_ReaScriptAPI and OSARA are optional; they add features where available.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 What is included\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ZP Studio Suite} \u8212- teleprompters, SRT import/export and references, project tools, mixdown preparation, voice-minute reports, Voice Cleaner and accessible workflows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ZP Voce} \u8212- voice chains, dialogue tools and voice/music processing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ZP Master} \u8212- mastering and reference-tone tools.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ZP Misura} \u8212- loudness meters, oscilloscope, passive signal probes and ZP BrownSlope Prism, a passive brown-slope analyzer.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Version 2.6.6 adds automatic copying and Sync now in Render & Copy on Windows (requires js_ReaScriptAPI) and Linux (requires find and stat). Version 2.6.5 updates the Solo Recorder guide to explain how ZP Remote packages relate to Dubbertools. Version 2.6.4 added Render & Copy, a Dubbertools link in SOLO Web, and the ZP Remote REAPER tool for creating packages and importing deliveries. ZP Remote export requires Python 3 and ffmpeg.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Version 2.6.9 introduces {\b ZP Shared Bus v3.1}, the new {\b {\f1 39 ZP Telemetry Engine}}, the new {\b {\f1 ZP Spoken Finish Pro 1.0.0}} (shipped alongside classic {\f1 ZP Spoken Finish 3.10.2} with the {\f1 MAGIC} {\f1 VELVET \u183 ? AIR SILK \u183 ? 3D FOCUS} signature module), {\b {\f1 30 ZP SRT 2.0}} (unified 4-tab subtitle workstation with {\f1 Coalesce short cues}), two calibrated {\b Project Templates} ({\f1 -18 LUFS} VoiceOver and {\f1 -8 LUFS} Mix-Spot), {\b {\f1 ZP Master Pro 2.52}} ({\f1 TRANSP} transparent profile + {\f1 ENHANCE} + {\f1 2\u215 ? PRECLIP} + {\f1 SPT -8 LUFS} preset and {\b CATENA} tab), {\b {\f1 ZP BUS Chain 1.3.7}} (Teletronix LA-2A Gray-calibrated {\f1 LA2 GRAY} + {\f1 PAD -6} + {\f1 2\u215 ?} oversampling), {\b {\f1 ZP Magic Voice LAB 1.2.7}} ({\f1 20 kHz} linear transparency via residual-only 2\u215 ? oversampling and 5 UAD-calibrated hardware cartridges), {\b {\f1 ZP Click & Attack Softener 1.4}} (STFT spectral {\f1 MICRO-CLICK} with {\f1 ~940 Hz} local pocket coherence, continuous {\f1 Freq Skew} {\f1 Low \u8596 ? Air}, and automatable {\f1 Micro %}), {\b {\f1 ZP Loudness Meter Multichannel 45.3}}, {\b {\f1 ZP BrownSlope Prism 1.2}} (cepstral comb-filter detection), {\b {\f1 ZP Audition Noise Monitor 1.1}} (Monitor FX), and unified product branding ({\f1 latocardioide.it \u183 ? dubbertools.com}) across all Lua windows, JSFX plugins, and IT/EN guides.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ZP Studio Suite 2.6.7 distributes {\b ZP Magic Voice LAB 1.2.0-lab3}, the correct version, as a separate {\b ZP Voce} effect. {\b ZP Magic Voice 1.2.0} without LAB is an archived prototype and is excluded from the package. Install ZP Magic Voice LAB alongside ZP Studio Suite in ReaPack. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ZP%20Studio%20Suite/help/en/magic_voice_lab.html"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Operating guide
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Version 2.6.8 includes: {\b Embed into Items} will copy only timeline markers you have selected; operational markers such as Harmonic Space Carver's {\f1 #HSC} cues will stay on the timeline. It also includes {\b ZP Magic Voice LAB 1.2.3} (backward-compatible DRC {\f1 FREQ} center + {\f1 OCT} octave width knobs, real continuous response curves in {\f1 DRC}, {\f1 DYN EQ} {\f1 \u177 ?5 / \u177 ?12 dB} and {\f1 DYN BAL} {\f1 \u177 ?6 / \u177 ?12 dB} monitors, flashing global DELTA with 30 s auto-off, extended spring-loaded per-stage {\f1 S\u183 ?DELTA}, 4 s active-speech block suggestions, color-only {\f1 LIGHT / DARK} theme keeping all DRC controls visible), {\b ZP BrownSlope Prism 1.1} ({\f1 \u177 ?1.5 / \u177 ?3 dB} tolerance corridor, warm/cool differential fill, optional {\f1 Live} trace, bipolar zone bars, slope spirit level, and Dark/Light theme toggle), {\b ZP Loudness Meter Multichannel 45.0} (vertical-first anti-drift UI with free {\f1 TARGET} + one-click {\f1 LOCK NOW}, green {\f1 \u177 ?LU} band, 60s drift ribbon freezing on pause, floating peak-hold, 4 responsive views including {\f1 LUFS-I}/{\f1 TP} embedded TCP/MCP, and Dark/Light themes) and the {\b scrollable {\f1 STATO} log} in {\b ZP Render & Copy}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ZP Studio Suite 2.6.7 adds ZP Consolidate, which copies referenced take sources and project-registered SRT/VTT files into Media without converting media. See the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "CHANGELOG.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
changelog
}}}
 for the complete list of changes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Separate packages\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Starting with 2.6.9, these packages have graduated from BETA (2026-11-26); the requirements and limits stay as listed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ZP Clean & Paint}: ReaPack installs the REAPER actions. The ZP Voice Model Lab engine, Python environment, presets and voice models remain external and must be installed and configured separately.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ZP Montaggio Parlato}: requires ZP Studio Suite and ZP Speech from 33 Welcome; the current version is tested on macOS. PDF import needs {\f1 pdftotext} (Poppler). Clipboard paste needs SWS.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ZP BrownSlope Dynamic Guard} and {\b ZP Click & Attack Softener}: separate effects to try on sessions and working copies. Cue Navigator is only needed for the {\f1 ?} help button.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ZP Speech (the transcription engine behind Transcribe, 29) is not in the ReaPack package: install it from Welcome (33), which downloads it from GitHub. On macOS it uses MacWhisper or OpenAI Whisper; on Windows and Linux it uses local OpenAI Whisper and is still {\b experimental}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Guides and source\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ZP%20Studio%20Suite/help/en/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
English Suite guide
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ZP%20Studio%20Suite/help/en/lab.html"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Separate packages guide
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ZP%20Studio%20Suite/help/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Guida italiana della Suite
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://latocardioide.it/strumenti/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Website: Lato Cardioide \u8212- Tools
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/capitanpaolone/zp-suite/raw/master/index.xml"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack repository index
}}}
\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The ReaPack package description and release notes are provided in both English and Italian. The GitHub README is English-first; Italian readers can choose the Italian README and set the Suite language in {\b 33 Welcome}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 License and Disclaimer of Warranty\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Most components are licensed under {\b GPL-3.0-or-later}; some REAPER-derived meters are {\b LGPL-2.1-or-later}. See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "LICENSE"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
